LOCATION:Royale\, 279 Tremont St\, Boston\, MA 02116
DESCRIPTION:with Ben Caplan\nIf you ever feel as if music has lost its capa
 city for surprise\, the beguiling wonder and infinite creativity of Yaelok
 re will respark your belief. The Filipino-Icelandic artist - real name Kea
 th Ósk (they/it) - fuses three imaginative strands to their visionary exp
 ression: intimate\, innocent folk infused with leftfield surrealism and in
 stant pop accessibility\; artwork which is intricately detailed and beauti
 fully alluring\; and storytelling which brings personal experience and poe
 try into rich\, fable-like narratives. What’s more\, all three of these 
